    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nFor Sale by DNG Online Auction TO REGISTER FOR OUR ONLINE AUCTION on the 3rd December 2026 at 12pm.Visit www.dngauctions.ieChoose/ Search for your property of interest, click log in & register to bid and follow the necessary steps.Bidder security required prior to auction date in order to successfully bid on the day.DNG Martin O'Connor Land Sales are delighted to offer for sale by DNG Online Auction a holding of grazing lands together with undivided commonage interests, situated in the scenic Rusheeny Valley on the outskirts of Oughterard Village.The lands are contained within Folio GY4010F and comprise a number of separate parcels. File Plan 88 0.45 Ha (1.11 acres), File Plan 89 0.53 Ha (1.30 acres), File Plan 90 0.68 Ha (1.68 acres),File Plan 82 1.43 Ha (3.53 acres). File Plan 85 is also included in the sale, with its stated area not currently available. (Less than 0.20 acres)Total Land = c. 3.08 Ha (7.62 Acres)The holding further includes interests in two areas of commonage. File Plan 71 has a stated overall area of approximately 223.52 Ha (552.32 acres), in which a 96/711th undivided share is included in the sale = 30.18 Ha (74.57 Acres). File Plan 9 extends to approximately 1.65 Ha (4.07 acres), in which a 1/8th undivided share is included =0.20 Ha (0.508 Acres) Total undivided Commonage share = 30.38 Ha (75.08 Acres)The lands provide useful grazing in an established agricultural area and represent an attractive opportunity for farmers, adjoining landowners or those seeking to establish or expand an existing holding in the Oughterard area.\n\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment. The successful bidder is required to pay the balance of 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid.Directions: From Oughterard village proceed along Main Street towards Clifden passing the Garda Station on your left. Just before the Bridge turn left at McNamaras Shop & the Beauty House salon it will be signposted Costelloe and Shannapheasteen. Drive out this road past the Oughterard Motors and take the next right turn onto the Rusheeny Road. Driving for about a quarter of a mile and take a tuning to a house with Eircode H91NWV4, the commonage land surrounds this property and across the road up the Hill. Please use the maps to find the location of the other lots associated with this property."
      },
      {
